  "title": "Support for distress associated with climate change in Finland – “The mind of eco-anxiety”",
  "summary": "Established by mental health professionals, The \"Mind of Eco-Anxiety\" project in Finland recognizes eco-anxiety as a societal phenomenon. The initiative employs three pillars: awareness campaigns, mental health support, and education for professionals. It has reached millions through campaigns and involved hundreds in workshops. Even though climate change substantially influences mental health and well-being , attention to this issue in science and practice has been limited. Climate- or eco-anxiety are emerging concepts describing the distress linked to environmental and climate change.",
